{#- Analytics is OFF until analytics.provider is set in content.json.
    No script, no cookies, nothing loaded.

    There are deliberately NO inline <script> blocks here — the site's CSP
    forbids inline scripts, so anything that needs initialising is handed to
    main.js through a meta tag instead.

    Plausible sets no cookies and stores no personal data, so it needs no
    consent banner. GA4 does, and has one: cookie-banner.njk. -#}
{%- if tps.analytics.provider == "plausible" and tps.analytics.plausibleDomain %}
<script defer data-domain="{{ tps.analytics.plausibleDomain }}"
        src="https://plausible.io/js/script.tagged-events.outbound-links.js"></script>
{%- elif tps.analytics.provider == "ga4" and tps.analytics.ga4MeasurementId %}
{#- UK PECR: GA4 sets cookies, so it must not load before consent. Only the
    ID is handed over here; main.js loads gtag.js after "Accept" and never
    otherwise. -#}
<meta name="ga4-measurement-id" content="{{ tps.analytics.ga4MeasurementId }}">
{%- endif %}
